/*
  Reproduction: 1D edge tilting with interfacial DMI.
  Cortes-Ortuno et al., arXiv:1803.11174, Table I and Fig. 1a.

  Units      : SI throughout (m, A/m, J/m, J/m2, J/m3)
  Mesh       : 800x1x1 cells of 0.125 nm  (the paper states 1 nm on p.4; refined
               here to show the answer is converged, see mx3-check)
  Materials  : Aex 13e-12, Dind 3e-3, Msat 0.86e6, Ku1 0.4e6  -- ALL STATED, p.3
  Assumed    : alpha = 1        (not stated; static problem, damping only sets
                                 how fast Relax() converges, not the answer)
               m = Uniform(0,0,1) (not stated; along the stated easy axis)
  Numerics   : EnableDemag = false -- the paper states it excludes the
                 demagnetising field (p.7) and its Eq. 5 has no magnetostatic term
               OpenBC = true -- the paper's boundary condition (Eq. 11,
                 dTheta/dx = 1/xi) is the free-spin condition. mumax3's default
                 closed boundary gives 28 deg instead of 41 deg. This is a
                 model-matching choice, NOT a fit.
  Outputs    : edge cell and centre cell, for the analytic comparison
  Unverified : that alpha and the initial state reach the same minimum the
               paper's shooting method found. Both edges are assumed decoupled
               (100 nm wire vs 5.7 nm decay length).
*/

SetGridSize(800, 1, 1)
SetCellSize(0.125e-9, 0.125e-9, 0.125e-9)

Msat  = 0.86e6
Aex   = 13e-12
Ku1   = 0.4e6
anisU = vector(0, 0, 1)
Dind  = 3e-3
alpha = 1

EnableDemag = false
OpenBC      = true

m = Uniform(0, 0, 1)

// Crop to a single cell so its value lands in table.txt. Note this reports the
// cell CENTRE, half a cell in from the physical edge -- worth 0.1 deg here.
TableAdd(Crop(m, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1))
TableAdd(Crop(m, 400, 401, 0, 1, 0, 1))

Relax()
TableSave()
Save(m)
